decision: changes-requested

The review found one medium blocker and two low reporting defects:

- **Medium blocker — N1:** [review_dispatch.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2555068651/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:979) silently falls back to reviewer-controlled environment matching if the Linux CLI cannot set up the shim.
- **Low follow-up — N2:** [review_shim_linux.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2555068651/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go:219) can report a PID as reaper-terminated when pidfd returns `ESRCH`.
- **Low follow-up — N3:** [delegate.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2555068651/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go:1149) says a recovered run was failed even when release completes an already-recorded run with a different status.

The focused regression tests and `go vet` passed. Strict validation could not run its Go checks because the read-only sandbox denied temporary build-directory creation and cache access; the sealed bundle contains passing validation evidence for the scoped component. The strict surface check passed. The conclusion draft check accepted the draft. Rules applied: Go backend, security, and documentation style; workflow `.pose/workflows/review.md`.

In the POSE block, `finding` marks criteria that failed.

